Feature: Integration test scenarios for ProductController API

Scenario: Retrieve all products using HTTP GET method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  When I send a GET request to '/products'
  Then the response status should be 200
  And the response should be a list of products

Scenario: Create a new product using HTTP POST method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And the request body contains:
    """
    {
      "name": "Test Product",
      "description": "A product used for testing",
      "price": 29.99
    }
    """
  When I send a POST request to '/products'
  Then the response status should be 201
  And the response body should contain the product details:
    """
    {
      "id": "<auto-generated-id>",
      "name": "Test Product",
      "description": "A product used for testing",
      "price": 29.99
    }
    """

Scenario: Retrieve product by ID using HTTP GET method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And a product exists with ID 1
  When I send a GET request to '/products/1'
  Then the response status should be 200
  And the response body should contain the product details:
    """
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Test Product",
      "description": "A product used for testing",
      "price": 29.99
    }
    """

Scenario: Update an existing product using HTTP PUT method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And a product exists with ID 1
  And the request body contains:
    """
    {
      "name": "Updated Product",
      "description": "An updated product",
      "price": 39.99
    }
    """
  When I send a PUT request to '/products/1'
  Then the response status should be 200
  And the response body should contain the updated product details:
    """
    {
      "id": 1,
      "name": "Updated Product",
      "description": "An updated product",
      "price": 39.99
    }
    """

Scenario: Delete a product by ID using HTTP DELETE method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And a product exists with ID 1
  When I send a DELETE request to '/products/1'
  Then the response status should be 200
  And the response body should be empty

Scenario: Attempt to retrieve a product that doesn't exist using HTTP GET method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And no product exists with ID 999
  When I send a GET request to '/products/999'
  Then the response status should be 404
  And the response body should be empty

Scenario: Attempt to update a product that doesn't exist using HTTP PUT method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And no product exists with ID 999
  And the request body contains:
    """
    {
      "name": "Non-existent Product",
      "description": "This should fail",
      "price": 0
    }
    """
  When I send a PUT request to '/products/999'
  Then the response status should be 404
  And the response body should be empty

Scenario: Create a product with invalid input using HTTP POST method
  Given the API base URL 'http://localhost:8080'
  And the request body contains:
    """
    {
      "name": "",
      "description": "Invalid product details",
      "price": -10
    }
    """
  When I send a POST request to '/products'
  Then the response status should be 400
  And the response body should contain details of the validation error
